nv-certify-null-sign-handle-digest: unsigned NV digest attestations use the hash of inScheme

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Part 3 (version 185), TPM2_NV_Certify: "If size and offset are both zero and
signHandle is TPM_RH_NULL, the digest is computed using the hash algorithm
provided in inScheme, unless the scheme or hash algorithm is TPM_ALG_NULL, in
which case the TPM shall return TPM_RC_SCHEME." (Versions 1.83 and earlier
allowed an Empty Buffer.) Version 185 sets inScheme to TPM_ALG_NULL while
selecting the scheme for a NULL signHandle (CryptoCommon_SelectSignScheme())
and then takes the digest's hash algorithm from it, so it always returns
TPM_RC_SCHEME. The caller's scheme is kept for the digest.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/NVStorage/NV_Certify.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/NVStorage/NV_Certify.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/NVStorage/NV_Certify.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/NVStorage/NV_Certify.c
@@ -36,6 +36,14 @@ TPM2_NV_Certify(NV_Certify_In*  in,  // IN: input parameter list
     // Input Validation
     if(!IsSigningObject(signObject))
         return TPM_RCS_KEY + RC_NV_Certify_signHandle;
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // Part 3 (version 185), TPM2_NV_Certify: if size and offset are both zero and
+    // signHandle is TPM_RH_NULL, the digest is computed with the hash algorithm of
+    // inScheme, unless the scheme or hash algorithm is TPM_ALG_NULL, in which case
+    // the TPM returns TPM_RC_SCHEME (versions 1.83 and earlier returned an Empty
+    // Buffer). The scheme selection clears inScheme for a NULL signHandle, so the
+    // caller's scheme is kept.
+    TPMT_SIG_SCHEME callerScheme = in->inScheme;
     if(!CryptoCommon_SelectSignScheme(signObject, &in->inScheme))
         return TPM_RCS_SCHEME + RC_NV_Certify_inScheme;
 
@@ -92,7 +100,8 @@ TPM2_NV_Certify(NV_Certify_In*  in,  // IN: input parameter list
         TPMI_ALG_HASH hashAlg;
         HASH_STATE    hashState;
 
-        hashAlg = CryptoCommon_GetSignSchemeHashAlg(&in->inScheme);
+        hashAlg = CryptoCommon_GetSignSchemeHashAlg(
+            signObject == NULL ? &callerScheme : &in->inScheme);
         if(hashAlg == TPM_ALG_NULL)
         {
             return TPM_RCS_SCHEME + RC_NV_Certify_inScheme;
